{
  "subtype": "causal_attribution",
  "outcome_variable": "regional_cluster",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "Industry",
      "causal_role": "treatment",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Industry is a plausible candidate cause of regional location: firms cluster geographically by sector (e.g., semiconductors in South Bay). It functions as the treatment whose effect on region is being attributed. Not named in the query."
    },
    {
      "name": "Region_Cluster",
      "causal_role": "outcome",
      "named_in_query": true,
      "rationale": "This is the focus/outcome variable itself (regional_cluster), directly named in the query as the thing to be explained."
    },
    {
      "name": "Is_VC_Firm",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Being a VC firm could plausibly influence both the type of activity (a proxy for the treatment) and the region chosen (VCs cluster on Sand Hill Road / Peninsula). However it is largely a subset/attribute of Industry (VC/Investment appears as an industry value), so it partly overlaps the treatment rather than being a clean common cause. Weak confounder."
    },
    {
      "name": "Global_Presence",
      "causal_role": "collider",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Global presence is more plausibly a downstream consequence of a firm's industry and size and possibly its location, not a common cause of both industry and region. It looks like an outcome/collider, so treating it as a confounder would be an error."
    }
  ],
  "treatment_present": true,
  "treatment_columns": ["Industry"],
  "confounders": [
    {"name": "Is_VC_Firm", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.3}
  ],
  "confounder_quality": 0.2,
  "rationale": "The set does supply a plausible treatment (Industry) and re-adds the outcome (Region_Cluster). However it lacks genuine confounders: variables that cause BOTH industry AND region and must be adjusted to avoid bias. Is_VC_Firm overlaps with the treatment (it is essentially an industry indicator) rather than being an independent common cause, and Global_Presence is a downstream collider/outcome, not a confounder. No firm-founding-era, founder-origin, firm-size, funding-stage, or historical/agglomeration variables were surfaced from the text to control for common causes of both locating decisions and sector. So while a treatment is present, the causal-attribution claim -- surfacing non-obvious confounders that are common causes of treatment and outcome -- is essentially not realised."
}
```

